//? Title: Symbolic Cholesky: actual natural-order structural fill
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Symbolic elimination connects higher neighbors of each eliminated vertex. Actual
inserted fill edges explain the structural lower pattern for the original5 by5
grid, while numerical cancellation and ordering choices remain explicit
qualifications.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

At column k collect current neighbors with index greater than k. Emit k in each
corresponding lower row, then connect every pair of higher neighbors into a
clique. Newly absent pairs are actual fill edges; already connected pairs still
cost insertion-test work. Natural ordering is fixed. The result is potential
structural nonzero support for a generic SPD matrix, not a guarantee against
exact numerical cancellations and not a numerical Cholesky factorization.
Ordered sets add logarithmic insertion costs; pair attempts may be cubic in
vertex count and fill storage quadratic.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/symbolic_cholesky_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::symbolic_cholesky_trace({{1, 2}, {0}, {0}});
    std::print("| actual eliminated column | current higher neighbors | actual newly inserted edges | " "cumulative pairs |\n| ---: | --- | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | `{}` | `{}` | {} |\n", s.column, s.higher, s.fill,
                   s.cumulative_pairs);
    std::print("Actual structural lower rows `{}`.\n", r.lower);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Star pattern centered at column0");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual higher-neighbor pairs",
                                     r.pair_tests));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual new fill edges {}", r.fill));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/symbolic_cholesky_tiny.svg");
}
```
