> API and interpretation

Neighbor IDs are completely checked; patterns are symmetrized by union, loops
ignored and duplicates removed. The solver performs no ordering optimization and
cannot certify positive definiteness from an adjacency pattern. Original and
actual fill coordinates are separated directly from native producer outputs; no
report-side elimination reconstructs the red points.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Rose, Triangulated Graphs and the Elimination Process, Journal of Mathematical
  Analysis and Applications32 (1970),597-609

